 "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16241, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XF57F4oDNCeZdDCcqV35qL", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19368, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Shq4grMesGmEUwZkF8NiRR", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18). Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.2.9 and v2.3.0 were healthy; v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were unhealthy). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A retry of the same rollback completed. All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 has a healthy production history. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure, and confirm v2.3.1 is blocked from redeploy until fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 49968, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Shq4grMesGmEUwZkF8NiRR", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 49968, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Shq4grMesGmEUwZkF8NiRR", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 51760, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_017uwTrc1mdvJbvduE5Ghuag", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52060, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017uwTrc1mdvJbvduE5Ghuag", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52060, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017uwTrc1mdvJbvduE5Ghuag", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 54161, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were unhealthy, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Rollback issues:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the fleet mixed. I retried the same rollback once and it completed across all regions.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as SEV2 for checkout-api. The create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying and found INC-0001 already recorded with the full summary. I did not create a second incident, so on-call was paged only once.\n\nStill open: the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, the orchestrator partial failure, and whether v2.3.1 should be blocked from redeploy until it is fixed. These are listed as follow-ups in the incident.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011oQ8hsXd4Eb3xH6vBP3mix", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01SgBC6w5UNFAfQ5jn2jGUDv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0 (seq 1). v2.3.1 is the unhealthy release now running in all regions. Since v2.3.0 has been healthy in production, it doesn't need change-manager approval. Rolling back now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MRL6XDPjtdEiXqcNZPBNoC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback reported a partial failure. I'll check the current state before doing anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0155XxDJdM8iG8Fj1SagVKn7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout stopped after us-east, so the fleet is now mixed: us-east is on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. The original instruction was to roll back in all regions, so I'll retry the same rollback once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KBjiTUMBoNGLa5MLLNs6RK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XF57F4oDNCeZdDCcqV35qL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback succeeded on retry and all three regions are healthy on v2.3.0. Now I'll open the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Shq4grMesGmEUwZkF8NiRR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18). Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.2.9 and v2.3.0 were healthy; v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were unhealthy). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A retry of the same rollback completed. All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 has a healthy production history. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure, and confirm v2.3.1 is blocked from redeploy until fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying to avoid paging on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017uwTrc1mdvJbvduE5Ghuag", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were unhealthy, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Rollback issues:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the fleet mixed. I retried the same rollback once and it completed across all regions.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as SEV2 for checkout-api. The create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying and found INC-0001 already recorded with the full summary. I did not create a second incident, so on-call was paged only once.\n\nStill open: the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, the orchestrator partial failure, and whether v2.3.1 should be blocked from redeploy until it is fixed. These are listed as follow-ups in the incident.", "type": "text"}]}]}